---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Audubon Park | Claire Nyquist"
    description="Every species occurrence recorded in GBIF for the Audubon Park neighborhood of Northeast Minneapolis, each drawn as line art of the organism itself, chickadees to slime molds, colored by lifeform on a minimalist basemap, with filters per group."
>
    <div class="px-4 py-8">
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <div class="text-center mb-8">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl name-gradient mb-4">
                Audubon Park
            </h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
                Every species occurrence recorded in the Global Biodiversity
                Information Facility for the Audubon Park neighborhood of
                Northeast Minneapolis, mapped where it was observed.
            </p>
            <p
                class="text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-4xl mx-auto leading-relaxed mt-4"
            >
                This visualization celebrates biodiversity on Earth by
                examining a small sampling of the creatures in my own
                backyard. Each icon marks a spot where a species was recorded, drawn as
                what it is, from chickadees and bumble bees to milkweed and
                some seventy other shapes, and tinted with the species&rsquo;
                estimated dominant color: cardinal red, blue-jay blue,
                goldfinch gold, monarch orange. Click
                any icon for the species behind it, with a photo where an
                observer shared one. Species recorded at the very same spot
                are scattered with a little jitter so each one stays visible,
                and where too many crowd together they gather into a light
                gray circle showing the number of species; click it or zoom
                in to spread them out.
                Click a group in the legend to show only that group; click it
                again to bring everything back.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Legend -->
        <div
            id="legend"
            class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2 mb-4 text-sm text-gray-700"
        >
        </div>

        <!-- Map: full-bleed across the browser window -->
        <div style="width:100vw; margin-left:calc(50% - 50vw);">
            <div
                id="map"
                class="w-full border-y border-gray-200"
                style="height: 90vh; min-height: 600px; background:#fafafa;"
            >
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1 text-center sm:hidden">
                Use two fingers to move the map.
            </p>
            <p id="stat-line" class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 text-center"></p>
        </div>

        <!-- Sources & citations -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-10 text-xs text-gray-400 space-y-2">
            <p>
                <strong class="text-gray-500">Data:</strong> GBIF occurrence
                records queried within the OpenStreetMap boundary of the
                Audubon Park neighborhood, Minneapolis. Contributing datasets:
                the <a
                    href="https://www.gbif.org/dataset/4fa7b334-ce0d-4e88-aaae-2e0c138d049e"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600"
                    >eBird Observation Dataset</a
                > (<a
                    href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600">CC BY 4.0</a
                >) and the <a
                    href="https://www.gbif.org/dataset/82cb293c-f762-11e1-a439-00145eb45e9a"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600"
                    >Great Backyard Bird Count</a
                > (<a
                    href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600">CC0 1.0</a
                >) from the Cornell Lab of Ornithology, <a
                    href="https://www.gbif.org/dataset/50c9509d-22c7-4a22-a47d-8c48425ef4a7"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600"
                    >iNaturalist Research-grade Observations</a
                > (<a
                    href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600">CC BY-NC 4.0</a
                >), and 2015&ndash;2018 wild-bee survey records from the <a
                    href="https://www.gbif.org/dataset/8e02e1dd-ec54-405e-b4d7-7abdecd29cc7"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600"
                    >University of Minnesota Insect Collection</a
                > (<a
                    href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600">CC0 1.0</a
                >). GBIF reflects what observers have recorded
                and shared, not a complete inventory. Citation: GBIF.org (21
                August 2026), GBIF Occurrence Search, retrieved via the
                <a
                    href="https://techdocs.gbif.org/en/openapi/v1/occurrence"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600">GBIF API</a
                >. Global Biodiversity Information Facility,
                <a
                    href="https://www.gbif.org"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600">gbif.org</a
                >.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong class="text-gray-500">Photos:</strong> where an
                observer shared a photo with their record, the first
                available one is shown in that species&rsquo; popup, mostly
                iNaturalist observation photos distributed through GBIF. Each
                is credited to its photographer with a link to its <a
                    href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600"
                    >Creative Commons license</a
                >; photos remain the work of their observers.
                Not every record has one; eBird checklists, for example, are
                usually photo-free.
            </p>
            <p id="icon-citations">
                <strong class="text-gray-500">Icons:</strong>
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong class="text-gray-500">Basemap:</strong> &copy;
                <a
                    href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600"
                    >OpenStreetMap contributors</a
                >, tiles by
                <a
                    href="https://carto.com/attributions"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600">CARTO</a
                >. Neighborhood boundary from OpenStreetMap.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong class="text-gray-500">Built with:</strong>
                <a
                    href="https://leafletjs.com"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline hover:text-gray-600">Leaflet</a
                > with the Leaflet.markercluster and leaflet-gesture-handling
                plugins, and d3-dsv for CSV parsing.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <link
        rel="stylesheet"
        href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
    />
    <link
        rel="stylesheet"
        href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet.markercluster@1.5.3/dist/MarkerCluster.css"
    />
    <link
        rel="stylesheet"
        href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet-gesture-handling@1.2.2/dist/leaflet-gesture-handling.min.css"
    />
    <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
    ></script>
    <script
        is:inline
        src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet.markercluster@1.5.3/dist/leaflet.markercluster.js"
    ></script>
    <script
        is:inline
        src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet-gesture-handling@1.2.2/dist/leaflet-gesture-handling.min.js"
    ></script>
    <script is:inline src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/d3-dsv@3/dist/d3-dsv.min.js"
    ></script>

    <style is:global>
        .species-icon {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
        }
        .species-icon img {
            filter: drop-shadow(0 0 1.5px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9));
        }
        .cluster-badge {
            border-radius: 50%;
            background: rgba(243, 244, 246, 0.92);
            border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
            color: #4b5563;
            text-align: center;
            font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Inter, sans-serif;
            font-size: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
        }
        /* Shorter map on phones so the page still scrolls comfortably */
        @media (max-width: 640px) {
            #map {
                height: 65vh !important;
                min-height: 420px !important;
            }
        }
        /* The two-finger hint lives below the map instead of flashing
           over it on every one-finger swipe */
        .leaflet-gesture-handling-touch-warning:after {
            opacity: 0 !important;
        }
        #species-popup {
            position: absolute;
            transform: translate(-50%, -100%);
            z-index: 1100;
            width: 250px;
            background: #fff;
            border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
            padding: 10px 12px;
            font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Inter, sans-serif;
            font-size: 13px;
            line-height: 1.5;
        }
        #species-popup-close {
            position: absolute;
            top: 4px;
            right: 8px;
            font-size: 16px;
            color: #9ca3af;
            background: none;
            border: none;
            cursor: pointer;
            line-height: 1;
        }
        #species-popup-close:hover {
            color: #374151;
        }
    </style>

    <script is:inline>
        (function () {
            // One icon shape per lifeform (Claude-cropped line art, stored
            // as black-on-transparent masks); color marks the lifeform
            // group — Claire's palette, deep enough to read on the pale
            // basemap. Marker sizes preserve each drawing's aspect ratio.
            const GROUPS = [
                { key: "Birds", color: "#e13c30", icon: "birds", size: [22, 20], match: (d) => d.class === "Aves" },
                { key: "Insects", color: "#f2601a", icon: "insects", size: [22, 20], match: (d) => d.class === "Insecta" },
                { key: "Plants", color: "#2fae57", icon: "plants", size: [16, 20], match: (d) => d.kingdom === "Plantae" },
                { key: "Arachnids", color: "#d64fc4", icon: "arachnids", size: [20, 20], match: (d) => d.class === "Arachnida" },
                { key: "Mammals", color: "#c9a70a", icon: "mammals", size: [35, 16], match: (d) => d.class === "Mammalia" },
                { key: "Fungi", color: "#3186e0", icon: "fungi", size: [18, 20], match: (d) => d.kingdom === "Fungi" },
                { key: "Other", color: "#6d28d9", icon: "other", size: [26, 16], match: () => true },
            ];
            const groupOf = (d) => GROUPS.find((g) => g.match(d));

            // Species-specific icons: genus → drawing, from Claire's larger
            // Gemini line-art set. Anything unmatched falls back to its
            // lifeform's default icon above. Entries: [icon, [w,h], genera].
            const SUBICONS = {
                Birds: [
                    ["chickadee", [26, 20], "Poecile"],
                    ["cardinal", [16, 20], "Cardinalis"],
                    ["house-sparrow", [29, 20], "Passer Melospiza Spizella Spizelloides Zonotrichia Passerella Pipilo"],
                    ["crow", [23, 20], "Corvus"],
                    ["blackbird", [25, 20], "Agelaius Quiscalus Molothrus Sturnus"],
                    ["goldfinch", [25, 20], "Spinus Haemorhous Acanthis Passerina Pheucticus"],
                    ["woodpecker", [11, 20], "Dryobates Melanerpes Colaptes Dryocopus Sphyrapicus Leuconotopicus"],
                    ["robin", [23, 20], "Turdus Catharus Sialia Toxostoma Dumetella"],
                    ["blue-jay", [29, 20], "Cyanocitta"],
                    ["nuthatch", [19, 20], "Sitta Certhia"],
                    ["wren", [18, 20], "Troglodytes Thryothorus"],
                    ["swift", [27, 20], "Chaetura Hirundo Petrochelidon Riparia Tachycineta Chordeiles"],
                    ["mallard", [35, 16], "Anas Aix Spatula Lophodytes Gavia Phalacrocorax"],
                    ["dove", [24, 20], "Zenaida Columba"],
                    ["junco", [28, 20], "Junco"],
                    ["warbler", [28, 20], "Setophaga Leiothlypis Geothlypis Cardellina Mniotilta Seiurus Regulus Vireo Polioptila Empidonax Contopus Sayornis Myiarchus Tyrannus"],
                    ["hawk", [20, 24], "Accipiter Astur Buteo Falco Circus Haliaeetus Pandion Cathartes"],
                    ["turkey", [21, 24], "Meleagris"],
                    ["heron", [19, 28], "Ardea Butorides"],
                    ["hummingbird", [17, 14], "Archilochus"],
                    ["gull", [22, 20], "Larus Hydroprogne"],
                    ["killdeer", [24, 20], "Charadrius"],
                    ["oriole", [26, 20], "Icterus"],
                    ["waxwing", [20, 20], "Bombycilla"],
                    ["goose", [22, 22], "Branta Anser Cygnus"],
                    ["owl", [15, 22], "Bubo Strix"],
                    ["kingfisher", [14, 20], "Megaceryle"],
                    ["crane", [17, 28], "Grus"],
                ],
                Insects: [
                    ["bumblebee", [22, 16], "Bombus Pyrobombus"],
                    ["sweat-bee", [13, 16], "Agapostemon Halictus Melissodes Megachile Anthidium Colletes Coelioxys"],
                    ["miner-bee", [23, 16], "Andrena Calliopsis"],
                    ["monarch", [25, 18], "Danaus Vanessa Nymphalis Polygonia Speyeria Euptoieta Pieris Cyaniris Elkalyce Polites Epargyreus"],
                    ["swallowtail", [20, 18], "Papilio"],
                    ["ladybug", [13, 14], "Harmonia Hippodamia Coleomegilla"],
                    ["beetle", [14, 16], "Tetraopes Megacyllene Lucanus Chauliognathus Popillia Pelidnota Trirhabda Blepharida Labidomera Lilioceris Anthrenus Calomycterus Polydrusus Amphimallon Atalantycha Lucidota Creophilus Calymmaderus"],
                    ["grasshopper", [25, 14], "Melanoplus Dichromorpha Microcentrum Roeseliana"],
